        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T18:13:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One could impose short timeouts on each constituent operation, one long timeout on the entire SPI transaction, or both.\n\nI decided to do one timeout for the entire transaction for simplicity.  (See the comment above OCTOSPI_TRANSACTION_TIMEOUT_US on how I chose the value.)\n\nI do not expect this timeout to ever happen, because the progress is not dependent on anything external to EC microcontroller. (The SPI device cannot \"stretch the clock\" as on I2C, or otherwise affect the time it takes for the transaction to complete.)  So I do not think it is worth spending too much effort on the timeout logic.  The current logic will prevent the code from completely locking up, even if the SPI block is misbehaving somehow.",
      "parentUuid": "34285082_60b451ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 371,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 371,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "69076ef31b937b13aae0686fa431ee3d5f125798",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
