      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T18:13:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a good question what to do.  Basically, we can only get here in case of a code bug or hardware issue on HyperDebug, causing the OctoSPI controller to not initialize properly.\n\nYou are suggesting we should disable the other (non-Octo) SPI controller in such case?  I do not really see the point in that.\n\nWe could record the fact that initialization did not succeed, and maybe add some way for the Host computer to query via USB whether the EC board is properly initialized, but I do not feel that it is worth putting any effort into such an unlikely case.",
